<header class="page-header"><h1>Translate &amp; Fit for Illustrator</h1></header>

<p>Translate &amp; Fit is a tool for Adobe Illustrator. It exports the text of a document as XLIFF for a translation tool, imports the translated XLIFF into the same document, then lists the frames that overflow and fits them within limits you set.</p>

<ul>
<li><a href="https://aescripts.com/translate-fit-for-illustrator/">Script version on aescripts</a> (run from File &gt; Scripts)</li>
<li><a href="https://exchange.adobe.com/apps/cc/206152">Panel version on Adobe Exchange</a>, listed as Translate and Fit for Illustrator</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/linguist-coder/translate-fit">Free trial with a sample document on GitHub</a></li>
</ul>

<p><iframe loading="lazy" allowfullscreen title="Translate &amp; Fit for Illustrator, overview video" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/D9YV2OF9ml8"></iframe></p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
<li>Each paragraph is one translation unit. Bold, italic, color and size changes inside a paragraph travel as tags such as <code>&lt;g id="1"&gt;two years&lt;/g&gt;</code>, which the translator keeps around the matching words.</li>
<li>Threaded text frames are exported as one story, so a sentence that runs from one frame into the next stays in one unit.</li>
<li>Before it writes any text, import checks the XLIFF against the export and the current document: missing or unknown tags, paragraphs missing from the XLIFF, paragraphs edited after the export, and fonts that are not installed. If a check fails, it lists each problem with its paragraph and does not import.</li>
<li>Check overset lists the frames that overflow after import.</li>
<li>Fit tightens tracking first, then horizontal scale, then font size, and stops as soon as the text fits. A frame that cannot fit within your limits is put back as it was and listed.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What to know before you run it</h2>
<ul>
<li>Illustrator cannot undo the whole script run in one step. To discard an import or a Fit run, close the document without saving or choose File &gt; Revert.</li>
<li>Point text is not flagged by the overset check, so check by eye that translated headings still fit.</li>
<li>Text converted to outlines and text inside images are not exported.</li>
<li>Frames are not resized and other objects are not moved.</li>
<li>Right-to-left and vertical text have not been tested.</li>
<li>It works on the active document. It does not process a folder.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Trial</h2>
<p>The trial is a separate build and comes with a sample document, so you can run export, import and Fit from start to finish. Export, Check overset and pseudo-translation are unrestricted. Import and Fit have per-document limits. Pseudo-translation makes the text of your own XLIFF longer by a percentage you choose and keeps the tags, which shows how your layout responds before any real translation exists.</p>

<h2>Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Adobe Illustrator 2026 or later for the script version. The panel version supports Illustrator 2026.</li>
<li>Windows. macOS has not been tested, so try the free trial on your Mac before buying.</li>
<li>The document must be saved before you export, and the fonts for the translated text must be installed</li>
</ul>

